WEBVTT

1
00:00:17.845 --> 00:00:20.627
Saturday morning Ben floated through the kitchen.

2
00:00:21.487 --> 00:00:24.269
He was heading for the door when Uncle Bert stopped him.

3
00:00:24.289 --> 00:00:26.370
"You're just in time, Ben!"

4
00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:28.972
His uncle was floating near the stove, cooking.

5
00:00:29.512 --> 00:00:32.713
"I'm making my famous mudberry paincakes."

6
00:00:32.733 --> 00:00:38.034
"Paincakes?" Ben's stomach rumbled.

7
00:00:38.755 --> 00:00:42.596
"I was going to skip breakfast today, but I can't resist your paincakes."

8
00:00:42.616 --> 00:00:45.216
"Neither can anyone else."

9
00:00:46.277 --> 00:00:47.397
Uncle Bert laughed.

10
00:00:48.637 --> 00:00:52.439
"That's why I named my restaurant Bert's House of Paincakes."

11
00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:57.220
Ben sat down to eat.

12
00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:00.781
"Do you miss the restaurant since you sold it?"

13
00:01:02.182 --> 00:01:07.965
"Sometimes. But now I have time to travel, and I can take care of you and Sid when

14
00:01:08.005 --> 00:01:09.366
your parents go out of town.

15
00:01:09.887 --> 00:01:10.367
Eat up!"

16
00:01:10.767 --> 00:01:11.988
Uncle Bert smiled.

17
00:01:12.008 --> 00:01:15.430
"I tell you, Ben, you're a lucky ghost.

18
00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:18.912
Macdeath is my favorite Quakespeare play.

19
00:01:21.033 --> 00:01:24.375
And that's exciting about the professional actress who's directing the play.

20
00:01:24.875 --> 00:01:25.516
What's her name?"

21
00:01:27.004 --> 00:01:27.705
"Uncle Bert!"

22
00:01:28.045 --> 00:01:29.426
Sid yelled from upstairs.

23
00:01:29.446 --> 00:01:32.128
"Do I smell paincakes?"

24
00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:36.312
"You sure do," Uncle Bert called back.

25
00:01:36.332 --> 00:01:37.893
"Come get some, Sid!"

26
00:01:39.834 --> 00:01:42.436
Ben suddenly had a question for Uncle Bert too.

27
00:01:42.456 --> 00:01:43.758
"Hey, Uncle Bert.

28
00:01:43.998 --> 00:01:46.740
Do you know anything about the curse of Macdeath?

29
00:01:47.581 --> 00:01:49.122
Everybody keeps talking about it."

30
00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:53.385
"Curse?" Uncle Bert laughed.

31
00:01:53.405 --> 00:01:55.006
"There's no such thing."

32
00:01:55.026 --> 00:01:56.608
"Are you sure?"

33
00:01:57.792 --> 00:02:00.733
"Absolutely! That's pure superstition.

34
00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:06.174
I—" Uncle Bert knocked over the salt shaker with his flipper, sending salt flying.

35
00:02:07.235 --> 00:02:12.036
"Oops!" He quickly took a pinch of the spilled salt and threw it over his left shoulder.

36
00:02:12.056 --> 00:02:13.896
"Why'd you do that?"

37
00:02:14.316 --> 00:02:15.077
Ben asked.

38
00:02:15.877 --> 00:02:17.717
"Spilling salt is bad luck.

39
00:02:18.218 --> 00:02:20.338
This undoes it," Uncle Bert said.

40
00:02:20.358 --> 00:02:22.819
"But isn't that a superstition?"

41
00:02:23.019 --> 00:02:23.799
Ben asked.

42
00:02:23.819 --> 00:02:27.220
"Hmm Uncle Bert shrugged.

43
00:02:27.772 --> 00:02:28.452
"I guess so."

44
00:02:29.413 --> 00:02:33.295
The conversation was making Ben feel more worried about the school play.

45
00:02:34.196 --> 00:02:38.018
So he finished his stack of paincakes and picked up his script again.

46
00:02:38.038 --> 00:02:39.919
"Thanks for breakfast, Uncle Bert.

47
00:02:40.299 --> 00:02:42.400
I'll see you later—I have rehearsal all day today."

48
00:02:46.422 --> 00:02:51.825
When Ben arrived at Monster Academy, the cast and crew were waiting outside the auditorium.

49
00:02:51.845 --> 00:02:54.587
"What's going on?"

50
00:02:55.607 --> 00:02:56.728
Winnie looked annoyed.

51
00:02:57.752 --> 00:02:58.632
"We're locked out.

52
00:02:59.133 --> 00:03:03.494
I have to get to work on the cauldron and costumes, or nothing will be ready in time."

53
00:03:05.255 --> 00:03:06.516
Ben tugged on the doors.

54
00:03:06.536 --> 00:03:09.077
"Doesn't anybody have a key?"

55
00:03:09.097 --> 00:03:14.459
"Jen had a key, but she lost it," Jade muttered.

56
00:03:15.119 --> 00:03:16.340
Lucy rolled her eyes.

57
00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:18.421
"This is all her fault."

58
00:03:18.441 --> 00:03:20.762
"Yeah!" Sonia added.

59
00:03:23.363 --> 00:03:26.244
Jen was huddled in a corner, talking on her phone.

60
00:03:26.768 --> 00:03:31.090
She looked upset, and Ben guessed it had to do with the key situation.

61
00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:32.851
Just then Mr.

62
00:03:32.951 --> 00:03:33.831
Freaky arrived.

63
00:03:33.851 --> 00:03:35.212
"Step aside.

64
00:03:35.352 --> 00:03:36.892
Keys coming through!"

65
00:03:37.213 --> 00:03:38.293
Mr. Freaky called.

66
00:03:38.893 --> 00:03:41.915
As soon as the room was unlocked, everyone went inside.

67
00:03:41.935 --> 00:03:46.297
"I'm really sorry, Mr.

68
00:03:46.417 --> 00:03:47.877
Freaky," Jen said.

69
00:03:47.897 --> 00:03:50.438
"I don't know how I lost the keys."

70
00:03:50.458 --> 00:03:53.400
"It's all right, Jen," Mr.

71
00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:54.080
Freaky said.

72
00:03:54.532 --> 00:03:56.993
"Sounds like it was just a bit of bad luck."

73
00:03:57.013 --> 00:03:58.413
"Bad luck?"

74
00:03:58.874 --> 00:04:00.414
a two-headed monster murmured.

75
00:04:00.434 --> 00:04:01.755
"Or the curse?"

76
00:04:03.235 --> 00:04:04.075
Ozzy grinned.

77
00:04:04.095 --> 00:04:05.436
"I hope so!"

78
00:04:05.456 --> 00:04:08.237
"I hope not!"

79
00:04:08.797 --> 00:04:11.898
Mr. Freaky took out his handkerchief and blew his noses.

80
00:04:11.918 --> 00:04:14.099
"Ugh," Ben thought.

81
00:04:14.119 --> 00:04:16.600
"Here we go again with that dumb curse!"

82
00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:24.882
A few minutes later, Victoria Lafang arrived, looking glamorous as usual.

83
00:04:24.902 --> 00:04:28.323
"Good morning, my darling monsters!"

84
00:04:28.864 --> 00:04:29.444
she cried.

85
00:04:29.464 --> 00:04:32.805
"It's a new day, and we have a lot to do.

86
00:04:33.305 --> 00:04:37.027
We'll pick it up where we left off at our last rehearsal on Wednesday.

87
00:04:37.807 --> 00:04:38.968
Places, everyone!"

88
00:04:38.988 --> 00:04:42.829
"That's us," Jade said to her two friends.

89
00:04:42.849 --> 00:04:44.610
"You too, Ben."

90
00:04:47.451 --> 00:04:51.954
As Ben followed the three witches, Sonia's foot flew out from under her.

91
00:04:53.055 --> 00:04:55.437
She grabbed Lucy, who grabbed Jade.

92
00:04:57.138 --> 00:04:59.180
The three slammed to the floor.

93
00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:02.482
"Again!" Ben thought.

94
00:05:03.263 --> 00:05:05.545
On Wednesday the two zombies had slipped.

95
00:05:05.765 --> 00:05:08.347
Was the curse of Macdeath real after all?

96
00:05:08.367 --> 00:05:11.189
"Ugh!" Sonia cried.

97
00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:12.991
Winnie came running over.

98
00:05:13.011 --> 00:05:14.272
"Are you all right?"

99
00:05:14.884 --> 00:05:16.085
Jade snarled.

100
00:05:16.105 --> 00:05:18.448
"My dress is covered in slime!"

101
00:05:19.028 --> 00:05:19.989
Jen bit her lip.

102
00:05:20.009 --> 00:05:24.853
"My hair is slimy now!"

103
00:05:25.354 --> 00:05:26.094
Lucy cried.

104
00:05:26.114 --> 00:05:27.856
"What's going on?"

105
00:05:28.256 --> 00:05:29.377
Victoria demanded.

106
00:05:29.397 --> 00:05:32.460
"Why does everyone keep slipping on this stage?"

107
00:05:33.321 --> 00:05:34.422
Then she gasped.

108
00:05:35.963 --> 00:05:39.786
Glistening lines of slime zigzagged all over the stage.

109
00:05:39.806 --> 00:05:43.385
"Are those slime trails?

110
00:05:43.906 --> 00:05:45.507
On my stage?"

111
00:05:46.268 --> 00:05:47.209
Jen sighed.

112
00:05:51.072 --> 00:05:51.773
sorry, Ms.

113
00:05:51.813 --> 00:05:54.014
Lafang. I made them."

114
00:05:54.655 --> 00:05:55.936
She looked down at herself.

115
00:05:59.779 --> 00:06:00.840
can't help it!"

116
00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:03.823
"Oh, Jen darling!"

117
00:06:04.303 --> 00:06:06.565
Victoria draped her arm around Jen.

118
00:06:06.585 --> 00:06:09.828
"You're such a dear little stage manager.

119
00:06:10.272 --> 00:06:14.293
But I simply cannot have my actors slipping all over the stage.

120
00:06:14.953 --> 00:06:18.655
You're going to have find a solution, or I'll have to replace you.

121
00:06:19.155 --> 00:06:21.035
You understand, don't you?"

122
00:06:21.555 --> 00:06:22.336
Jen nodded.

123
00:06:22.356 --> 00:06:24.616
"I won't let you down, Ms.

124
00:06:24.656 --> 00:06:27.097
Lafang. And I'll clean up the slime."

125
00:06:27.117 --> 00:06:32.018
"Marvelous. Now let's begin with Ben's entrance onto the stage."

126
00:06:32.619 --> 00:06:34.099
Victoria turned to Ben.

127
00:06:34.119 --> 00:06:37.120
"I hope you're ready, Ben.

128
00:06:37.736 --> 00:06:42.303
No pressure, but as the lead character, this entire production rests on your shoulders."

129
00:06:42.604 --> 00:06:43.345
Ben gulped.

130
00:06:43.365 --> 00:06:45.308
"I'm ready, Ms.

131
00:06:45.348 --> 00:06:50.877
Lafang." He turned away for a second so she wouldn't see him wiping beads of sweat from his

132
00:06:50.937 --> 00:06:51.377
forehead.
